      <!-- ----- this is the interesting part of the page ----- -->
      <h3>Where can I get the source for iRogue?</h3>
      <P> The current version of iRogue is: 0.40.
      <P> <a href="iRogue.tar.gz">
      Download iRogue.tar.gz</a>

      <P> iRogue will be available at sourceforge.net "soon".

      <h3>What do I need to compile it?</h3>
      <P> iRogue requires prc-tools 2.0.  We compile under Linux, but
      other unices will probably also work.

      <P> You can get <a href="http://www.palmos.com/dev/tech/tools/gcc/">
      prc-tools 2.0</a> from <a href="http://www.palmos.com">
      palmos.com</a>.  Follow their
      directions for installation.  You will need
      <a href="http://www.ardiri.com/index.cfm?redir=palm&cat=pilrc">
      PilRC</a> as well (we are using version 2.5b5).

      <P> Since iRogue is large, it has "multiple code resources" and
      uses multigen.  You might want to read about that in the prc-tools
      documentation.

      <P> You may also want xcopilot, a Unix/X11 PalmPilot emulator.
      The xcopilot page is at <a href="http://xcopilot.cuspy.com/">
      http://xcopilot.cuspy.com/</a> and should have everything you
      need except a ROM image.


      
